            "entry": "pandas_ta/trend/zigzag.py",
            "changes": "The library's backtest flag is the Placement setting (Pivot = backtest off, the default; Detected = on). Swing window limited to 3 to 500 (the library's docstring asks for more than 2 legs; it accepts 1, a one-bar window where every bar is both a top and a bottom); deviation from 0.1. Output aligned to the input bars, null between swings, as the library; Detected points shifted forward by floor(legs / 2) bars, as the library's post-shift does, with those that would land past the last bar dropped (the library's roll wraps them to the first bars and then blanks them). The library's close argument, which it never reads, is not taken."
